WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:07.800
Artificial intelligence is developing rapidly. Every industry faces challenges brought by technology.

00:07.800 --> 00:14.500
The teaching field is no exception. The role of teachers and learning models will undergo changes.

00:14.500 --> 00:21.800
The Huang Kun-hui Education Foundation held a symposium on the 22nd, inviting scholars to explore this.

00:21.800 --> 00:29.000
Professor Inge Molenaar, Director of the National Education AI Lab at Radboud University, attended.

00:29.000 --> 00:36.000
She traveled from the Netherlands to Taiwan to share her research on AI applications in teaching.

00:36.000 --> 00:40.500
She discusses the transformation of educational systems and intensification of activities.

00:40.500 --> 00:50.000
"All of these system transformations went along with an extension of the educational system..."

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
"...and specifically an intensification of the educational activities within K-12."

01:00.000 --> 01:06.000
The seminar focuses on K-12 education reform in the AI era. AI empowerment is like a personal tutor.

01:06.000 --> 01:10.500
If students encounter difficulties, they can get answers at any time.

01:10.500 --> 01:14.000
Professor Huang Kun-hui believes this optimizes learning significantly.

01:14.000 --> 01:21.000
"How to make good use of AI to improve our curriculum, teaching methods, and assessment?"

01:21.000 --> 01:28.500
"To make teaching high-quality and become a smart, intelligent school."

01:28.500 --> 01:33.000
Technology changes with each passing day, and education must keep pace with the times.

01:33.000 --> 01:40.000
We hope AI-empowered education will become Taiwan's pride, just like semiconductor design.